--- A record made inside a function of the answers of two calls of one
--- function at two kinds holds each copy's answer: the first round read
--- the function's body with the kind a later call gave its parameter, and
--- the field kept that answer — the program was refused, "S's field 'a'
--- holds a list of bools, and this is numbers". A call that changes a
--- parameter's kind now answers nothing known until the body is read again
--- (Rosetta Code, Christofides algorithm).
struct S [a, b]

fn pair[n, value]
    return [value, value]

fn make[n]
    return S[pair[n, 0], pair[n, false]]

s = make[3]
log[s.a]
log[s.b]
